November is here and with a new month  comes a ton of new video games and this  week is home to a very anticipated  sequel that's Dishonored 2 this time  around you can play as corvo attano or  his daughter Emily each one has his own  set of abilities but both are out to  reclaim the throne in the coastal city  of car naka your decisions don't end  with choosing which character you'll use  as every mission is wide open for you to  take a stealthy or guns blazing approach  you can play as you see fit when  Dishonored 2 releases on November 11th  if you'd rather choose virtual reality  PlayStation VR is getting Eagle flight  it's one part post-apocalypse and one  part flight simulator the VR game lets  you control an eagle as it soars over  Paris 50 years after humans disappear  and nature reclaims the city you can  dive under bridges soar through narrow  alleys and even battle other birds and  multiplayer dogfights or will they  technically be Bird fights either way  that's out on the 8th let's return to  Earth for a moment with harvest moon Sky  Tree Village the latest in the cutesy  farming series lets you tend your crops  get married and start a family like  usual but this one also tasks you with  restoring the Lost Sky Tree Village to  do this you'll need to help the seven  legendary sky trees flourish and bring  prosperity back to the land you can  embark on this quest on your nintendo  3ds november eight if you prefer the  sword fighting world of high fantasy to  peaceful farms then you might like  tyranny the new RPG from obsidian a  rebellion has risen in the land of tears  and the powerful fate binder is set to  handle the situation you'll take on the  role of this fate binder acting as judge  jury and executioner as you make world  changing decisions complete quests and  grows stronger the journey begins on PC  on the 10  if you're in the market for a new  console you're in luck Sony's  PlayStation 4 pro takes the console  generation a step forward with enhanced  graphics 4k and HDR support and faster  processing and frame rates all current  ps4 games will work with the new system  and a bunch of them are getting updated  to look prettier and run better if you  want to upgrade or if you want your  first ps4 to be the fanciest you can  pick one up on the 10th and those are  the heavy hitters for this week as  always please remember that release  dates are based on retailer listings and  are subject to change we'll see you guys  back here next time
 

